// PARAM: --analysis congruence
// The stride loop from Mine's tutorial example 4.10: v starts at 1 and
// steps by 2 while v < 51, so v is exactly 51 on exit.
//
// Congruence holds the stride and nothing else. The loop head joins 1 and
// 3 into 1 (mod 2), v := v + 2 maps that class to itself, and the fixpoint
// is reached in one further step -- no widening needed, which is why the
// domain publishes join as its only solver discipline. The exit guard
// contributes nothing: inv_less_congruence is the identity, so !(v < 51)
// leaves the class untouched.
//
// The concrete mechanism losing v == 51 is therefore the lattice, not the
// transfer functions: a residue class carries a residue and a modulus and
// no magnitude, so 1 (mod 2) is the strongest statement available and
// congruence_eqb declines on it. The composite recovers the exact value --
// 16-composite-domain/precision/05-mine_ex410_stride2_congruence.vimp runs
// this same loop under --analysis int, where the interval narrows v to
// [51,52] and the congruence-to-interval reduction rounds that
// class-aligned to [51,51].
void main() {
  v := 1;
  while (v < 51) {
    v := v + 2
  };
  __voblint_check(v == 51) // UNKNOWN
}
